Description: PAM module that caches the login password into the user keyring
 pam_hkpac is a small PAM module which, during authentication, captures the
 user's login password and stores it into the user keyring (@u, key name
 "ACpass"), so that later single sign-on (SSO) consumers can reuse it without
 prompting the user again.
 .
 The module performs no authentication itself: it returns PAM_IGNORE, and the
 actual authentication is still carried out by the following modules
 (e.g. pam_deepin_authentication.so in common-auth).
 .
 Note: the PAM service configuration (e.g. /etc/pam.d/lightdm) must be updated
 separately to invoke this module.
